#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Write the audit view of an archived run: audit.json and audit.md.

usage:
  python3 audit RUN_FOLDER [--repo DIR] [--head REF] [--out DIR] [--json]

RUN_FOLDER is a history run folder (archive-run's layout): a *.lanes.json
manifest, the plan and spec copies, the *.ledger dir, and per launch its
wf_<id>.json result file and wf_<id>/ transcript dir. audit reads only that
folder: every input path is resolved (symlinks and junctions included) and
must lie inside it, a launch's result comes only from RUN_FOLDER/<wf>.json,
and no live path of the manifest (repo.root, repo.ledger_dir, plan, spec) is
ever read. It runs 'ledger status' on the archived ledger (for event facts
only) and check-verify in its archive mode (--ledger), keeping only
check-verify's status, a known reason code and its exit code.

--repo DIR is a worktree or a git dir holding the run's commits (in shadow
mode, repo.git_dir). Git is used read-only (--no-optional-locks, no fetch,
no config or ref change). A repo that lacks the run's start point is not
used: every git fact is then unavailable with the reason. Without --repo
every git fact is unavailable ("no --repo"). --head REF (needs --repo) is
the branch tip to compare against: the commits after the delivered sha are
listed under After delivery.

It writes audit.json and audit.md, as UTF-8, to --out (default
RUN_FOLDER/audit/), replacing only those two files, and prints a summary of
at most 10 lines whose last line is 'full report: <path of audit.md>' (with
--json it prints audit.json instead). The contract of both files is in
_audit.py: audit.json is {"audit_version": 3, "run_id", "repo", "run",
"tasks", "gaps", "gap_causes"}, every value a ref {"value", "state",
"sources"[, "note"]} and every recorded text a quote {"quote", "sources",
"commands_replaced"} in which configured commands are check ids; gaps lists
every value whose state is missing, stale, conflicting or unavailable, and
gap_causes the same gaps once per cause (the pointer with every array index
as N, the state, the note with its shas masked), with the ids of the tasks
holding it, or every value of a run-level one. The plan and spec hashes and
the plan copy's state are run-level: run.checks holds them once, and
audit.md prints them once under Checks. audit.md starts with a line saying
it holds local paths and recorded text and is not meant to be shared
as-is, then a Bottom line paragraph built only from values audit
computed (no recorded text), and ends with a Terms section defining its
labels. In audit.md, checks that ran and failed read 'failed checks'
(audit.json keeps invalid and the checks_failed rule), and a ruling
without a by reads 'implementer (no role recorded)'. What a launch's
journal (wf_<id>/journal.jsonl) records reads as recorded, cited by its
line ('<wf>/journal.jsonl L<n>'): the task review verdicts ('[present]',
with '(the engine read it as <x>)' where an engine from 1.2.0 acted on
another), the lens heads and the final re-review's head (the code outside
the task ranges it contains reads 'final re-review [present] - judged
<head7>'). Open work gives, under the final review line, the final
re-review line ('- final re-review: judged <head7>: <r> resolved, <o>
open, <m> without a result of the <F> final finding(s); <n> new',
open_work.final.value.re_review) and, after each final finding's
disposition, its re-review ('- re-review: <status>') with the
re-reviewer's evidence quoted; task minors have none. Neither needs
--repo. The summary's open work line and audit.md's Open work header count
'<open> open and <declined> declined final finding(s), <M> open task
minor(s)', M
being the result's task_minors_open plus its carried_minors_open ('<M> open
task minor(s) listed (more may be missing)' when the engine noted that some
minors did not reach the final lenses; unavailable when the result has
neither list, and Open work then says once that this run's engine recorded
none); each task block ends with the open minors its id prefix places
there, and a minor of a batch unit or of no task is under Open work only.
Each task block says whether the task's own check (its ledger's
checks/task-<unit>.<n>.json, engines from 1.6.0) ran before its commit, how
its last attempt ended and what it covered ('- checked before its commit:',
tasks[i].checks.task_check; run.checks.task_checks names the tasks an engine
before 1.6.0 committed and the files that match no task), never copying a
check file's error, tail, log or checkout; and its verified line says what
the containment covers ('its last commit <sha7> is in the head the
delivered verify passed at, <sha7>'). The task check needs no --repo. The
Bottom line adds 'task checks: <k> whose last check failed' when k > 0.
The summary's tasks line counts as the Bottom line does. For accepted by
user, the Bottom line names audit's verdict without the override when it
differs from the run's own (acceptance.verdict_without_override and
verdict_rule_without_override). When 'ledger status' failed, the open work
line's task count reads 'unknown (ledger status unavailable)'. The
summary, the Bottom line and the Evidence gaps header
say '<G> evidence gap(s) in <C> cause(s)', and Evidence gaps lists one line
per cause. The same inputs give the same bytes.

An --out that is RUN_FOLDER, is equal to or inside any *.ledger or wf_* dir
of the run, would make one (its first part under RUN_FOLDER matches *.ledger
or wf_*, whether or not that dir exists yet), or holds a *.lanes.json is
refused, and so is a default RUN_FOLDER/audit that resolves outside
RUN_FOLDER. Each file is written through a temp file that mkstemp creates
in --out, so an existing file or link there is never followed.

Exit 0 whenever the view is written (a folder with no launch, or a repo
without the run's start point, included); 2 on a usage error (--head without
--repo, an empty value), a RUN_FOLDER that is no directory or holds no
*.lanes.json, a refused --out, or an input that resolves outside RUN_FOLDER
(nothing is written), and when --out cannot be made or written ("cannot
write <out>: <error>"); 3 when a path needs converting on Windows and no Git
Bash or cygpath is found.
"""

import argparse
import fnmatch
import glob
import json
import os
import sys
import tempfile

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import _audit  # noqa: E402
import _audit_core  # noqa: E402
import _autopsy  # noqa: E402
import _shell  # noqa: E402

USAGE = "audit RUN_FOLDER [--repo DIR] [--head REF] [--out DIR] [--json]"


def _shown(path):
    return path.replace("\\", "/") if os.sep == "\\" else path


SOURCE_PATTERNS = ("*.ledger", "wf_*")


def _first_part(folder, out):
    """The first path component of out under folder (both resolved), or
    None when out does not lie inside folder."""
    if not _audit_core.inside(folder, out):
        return None
    try:
        rel = os.path.relpath(os.path.realpath(out), os.path.realpath(folder))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return rel.split(os.sep)[0]


def refused_out(folder, out):
    """Why out may not be written to, or None."""
    if _audit_core.inside(folder, out) and _audit_core.inside(out, folder):
        return "--out %s is the run folder" % _shown(out)
    pattern = glob.escape(folder)
    sources = [p for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(pattern, "*.ledger")) + glob.glob(os.path.join(pattern, "wf_*"))
               if os.path.isdir(p)]
    for path in sorted(sources):
        if _audit_core.inside(path, out):
            return "--out %s lies in the run's %s" % (_shown(out), os.path.basename(path))
    # A dir not made yet would be read as a launch or a ledger by the next
    # audit, autopsy or archive-run.
    first = _first_part(folder, out)
    if first is not None and any(fnmatch.fnmatch(first, p) for p in SOURCE_PATTERNS):
        return "--out %s would make %s in the run folder, which reads as a run source" % (_shown(out), first)
    if os.path.exists(out) and not os.path.isdir(out):
        return "--out %s is not a directory" % _shown(out)
    if os.path.isdir(out) and glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(out), "*.lanes.json")):
        return "--out %s holds a *.lanes.json" % _shown(out)
    return None


def write(out, name, text):
    """Write out/name through a new temp file in out: mkstemp creates it
    exclusively, so an existing file or link there is never followed."""
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=out, prefix=".audit-", suffix=".tmp")
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
            f.write(text)
        os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(out, name))
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.remove(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise


class Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    def error(self, message):
        print("audit: %s" % message, file=sys.stderr)
        print("usage: %s" % USAGE, file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)


def main(argv):
    _shell.setup_io()
    p = Parser(prog="audit", usage=USAGE, allow_abbrev=False)
    p.add_argument("run_folder")
    p.add_argument("--repo")
    p.add_argument("--head")
    p.add_argument("--out")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    args = p.parse_args(argv[1:])
    for name in ("run_folder", "repo", "head", "out"):
        if getattr(args, name) == "":
            p.error("%s is empty" % ("RUN_FOLDER" if name == "run_folder" else "--" + name))
    if args.head is not None and args.repo is None:
        p.error("--head needs --repo")

    try:
        folder = os.path.abspath(_shell.native_path(args.run_folder))
        repo = _shell.native_path(args.repo) if args.repo is not None else None
        out = os.path.abspath(_shell.native_path(args.out)) if args.out is not None else None
    except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
        print("audit: %s" % e, file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    if not os.path.isdir(folder):
        print("audit: not a directory: %s" % _shown(folder), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if _autopsy.find_manifest(folder) is None:
        print("audit: no *.lanes.json manifest in %s" % _shown(folder), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if out is None:
        out = os.path.join(folder, "audit")
        if os.path.lexists(out) and not _audit_core.inside(folder, out):
            print("audit: --out %s resolves outside the run folder; nothing written" % _shown(out),
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    reason = refused_out(folder, out)
    if reason is not None:
        print("audit: %s; nothing written" % reason, file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    try:
        audit = _audit.build(folder, repo=repo, head=args.head)
    except _audit_core.OutsideRunFolder as e:
        print("audit: %s; nothing written" % _shown(str(e)), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    json_text = json.dumps(audit, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
    md_text = _audit.render_md(audit)
    try:
        os.makedirs(out, exist_ok=True)
        write(out, "audit.json", json_text)
        write(out, "audit.md", md_text)
    except OSError as e:
        print("audit: cannot write %s: %s" % (_shown(out), e), file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if args.json:
        sys.stdout.write(json_text)
    else:
        sys.stdout.write(_audit.render_summary(audit, _shown(os.path.join(out, "audit.md"))))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv))
